`_isValidEmail` — regex RFC-lite: `^[\w.+-]+@[\w-]+(\.[\w-]+)+$`. Check against test cases:
- 'plainaddress' → no @ → invalid ✓
- 'a@b' → needs dot after domain → invalid ✓ (a@b: `[\w-]+(\.[\w-]+)+` requires at least one dot group → invalid ✓)
- 'foo@bar@baz.com' → two @ → invalid ✓
- 'user@example.com' → valid ✓
- 'google.user@gmail.com' → valid ✓ (dot in local part allowed)

